<p>
<font size=5>TAC Meeting</font><br>
<b>Linda Klein</b><br>
<i>LRK Communications</i>
<p>
<table cellpadding=2 cellspacing=2>
<tr>
	<td valign="top">
The Technical Advisory Committee (TAC) met at the project site on September 8th for the last on-site meeting of the field season.  Wayne Paradis (USFS, Grangeville), talked with the group about the McComas Meadows site and encouraged the exchange of information between projects.  During the remainder of the morning, the TAC performed the Low-Flow Field Review.  In the afternoon, Steve Bauer (PWI) provided attendees with a copy of the Final 1997 Monitoring Report and presented a 1998 monitoring activity update.                                                           
<p>
Peter Goodwin (UI) and Gloria Beattie (UI) used a slide show to explain UI engineering design philosophy, GIS technology, and project-related data input/map production.  Peter also described UI efforts to obtain outside funding to expand the educational component of our project.  Steve Clayton (UI) led the group in a discussion of Phase III (field season 1999) design criteria, preliminary conceptual ideas, and engineering challenges. 
	</td>
	<td valign="top" width="150" bgcolor=<%=color2%> align="center">
